# React Native (`react-native/`)

Expo **SDK 57** app for real DSA demos. Read `react-native/AGENTS.md` and https://docs.expo.dev/versions/v57.0.0/ before using Expo APIs.

## Stack

- expo-router: routes in `src/app/`; root layout wires `AppTabs`
- `@/*` → `src/*`; `@/assets/*` → `assets/*`
- React Compiler on — avoid unnecessary `useMemo` / `useCallback`

## Where code goes

| Kind | Path |
|------|------|
| Screens / routes | `src/app/` |
| UI | `src/components/` |
| DSA cores | `src/dsa/<feature>/` (pure TS, no React) |
| HTTP | `src/api/` (base URL: `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL`) |
| Theme | `src/constants/theme.ts` |

## Conventions

- Thin routes; call named DSA modules (e.g. trie, heap) with a short “why this DS?” comment or README in that folder.
- One API client; no scattered `fetch` with hardcoded hosts.
- No secrets in the bundle — only `EXPO_PUBLIC_*`.
- Explicit loading / error / empty UI for async screens.
- Do not block the JS thread with heavy algorithms.
